  "security_implications": "txcount is a transmission counter inside HMAC core that controls how many bytes are sent out, potentially including digest bytes. Corruption via glitch on txcount_d or improper reset could cause over-transmission of secret digest material or under-transmission leading to HMAC verification failure, leaking secret or causing denial-of-service. The asynchronous reset ensures a clean start.",
